The implementation now races deadlines without structured draining, retains any cancellation-ignoring work in a bounded registry, reports it in owned-resource snapshots, and cancels it during teardown. Upload no longer detaches the channel state machine: only the injected source read is raced, while a single absolute upload deadline is threaded through open/read/write/EOF/exit. I’ve added non-cooperative resolver and upload-source regressions.
